    {
     "q": "Why EDI instead of mixed-bed ion exchange?",
     "a": "EDI regenerates continuously with an electric field, so there are no acid or caustic deliveries, no regeneration downtime and no resin exhaustion events to investigate."
    },
    {
     "q": "Can the same skid feed a WFI still?",
     "a": "Yes. We size the skid for your PW draw plus the still's feed demand and meet the still maker's feed limits, typically on conductivity, silica and chlorine."
    },
    {
     "q": "How do you handle cold feed water in winter?",
     "a": "Canadian municipal water can fall to 2–5 °C in winter, which reduces RO output. We size membranes at your lowest feed temperature or add a heat exchanger to hold a design temperature."
